hadiths[87]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19477","Yahya narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, and Waki narrated to us, Yusuf narrated to us, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever does not trim from his mustache is not of us."
"19478","Waki narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to the people of Quba while they were praying Duha, and said: The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun in the forenoon."
"19479","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, Yazid ibn Hayyan al-Taymi narrated to me, he said: I set out with Husayn ibn Sabrah and Umar ibn Muslim to Zayd ibn Arqam, and when we sat with him, Husayn said to him: You met much good, O Zayd, you saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and heard his hadith, and raided with him, and prayed with him, you saw much good, O Zayd, narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O son of my brother, by Allah, I have grown old in age, my time is distant, and I forgot some of what I retained from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so what I narrate to you accept it, and what I do not, do not burden me with it, then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood one day addressing us at a water called Khumm between Makkah and Madinah, and he praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him and exhorted and reminded, then said: As for after, O people, I am only a man, about that the messenger of my Lord Almighty comes to me and I respond, and I leave among you two weighty things, the first of them is the Book of Allah Almighty, in it is guidance and light, so take the Book of Allah Almighty and hold fast to it, so he urged upon the Book of Allah and inclined toward it, he said: And my household, I remind you of Allah regarding my household, I remind you of Allah regarding my household, I remind you of Allah regarding my household, so Husayn said to him: Who are his household, O Zayd, are not his wives of his household, he said: His wives are of his household, but his household are those forbidden charity after him, he said: Who are they, he said: They are the family of Ali and the family of Aqil and the family of Jafar and the family of Abbas, he said: Were all these forbidden charity, he said: Yes."
"19480","Yazid ibn Hayyan said: Zayd ibn Arqam narrated to us in that sitting, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Ziyad sent to me and I came to him, and he said: What hadiths do you narrate and report from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which we do not find in the Book of Allah, you narrate that he has a basin in Paradise, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated it to us and promised us it, he said: You lied, but you are an old man who has doted, he said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell, and I did not lie upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"19481","And Zayd narrated to us in his sitting, he said: A man of the people of Fire will be made huge for the Fire until a molar of his molars is like Uhud."
"19482","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: A Jewish man bewitched the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: So he complained of that for days, he said: So Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: A Jewish man bewitched you, making knots for you in such and such well, so send one to bring them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and he extracted them and brought them and untied them, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood as if released from bonds, and he did not mention that Jew nor was it seen in his face ever until he died."
"19483","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Talhah, freedman of Qarazah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are not a part of a hundred thousand parts of those who come to my basin on the Day of Resurrection, he said: So we said to Zayd: How many were you then, he said: So he said: Between six hundred to seven hundred."
"19484","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: A Jewish man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Abu al-Qasim, do you not claim that the people of Paradise eat therein and drink, and he said to his companions: If he affirms this for me I will defeat him, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, one of them will be given the strength of a hundred men in food and drink and desire and intercourse, he said: So the Jew said to him: One who eats and drinks has need to relieve himself, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The need of one of them is sweat pouring from their skins like the scent of musk, then the belly is slimmed."
"19485","Ismail Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, that Zayd ibn Arqam saw people praying in the mosque of Quba in the forenoon, and said: They surely knew that prayer at other than this hour is better, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels feel the heat, and he said once: While people were praying."
"19486","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, he said: Zayd ibn Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas said to him, recalling: How did you inform me about meat gifted to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in pilgrim sanctity, he said: Yes, a man gifted him a limb of game meat, and he returned it and said: We do not eat it, we are in pilgrim sanctity."
"19487","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, that Zayd ibn Arqam used to magnify Allah four times over our funerals, and he magnified Allah five times over a funeral, and they asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to magnify them, or the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, magnified them."
"19488","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever does not trim from his mustache is not of us."
"19489","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Minhal, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling gold for silver on credit."
"19490","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, Bahz said in his hadith: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal, a man of Banu Kinanah, he said: I asked al-Bara about exchange, and he said: Ask Zayd ibn Arqam, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable, he said: So I asked Zayd, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19491","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar and Amir ibn Musab informed me, they heard Abu al-Minhal, he said: I asked al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam, then he mentioned like it."
"19492","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Abu al-Minhal, and he did not hear it from him, that he heard Zayd and al-Bara, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19493","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail, al-Harith ibn Shubayl narrated to me, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: A man used to speak to his companion in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a need in prayer, until this verse came down: And stand before Allah devoutly, so we were commanded silence."
"19494","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman, narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, he said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam and said to him: A relative by marriage of mine narrated to me from you a hadith about Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, on the day of Ghadir Khumm, and I love to hear it from you, and he said: You people of Iraq, in you is what is in you, and I said to him: There is no harm upon you from me, and he said: Yes, we were at al-Juhfah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us at noon holding the arm of Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and said: O people, do you not know that I am closer to the believers than themselves, they said: Yes, he said: Whomsoever I am his patron, Ali is his patron, he said: So I said to him: Did he say: O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him, he said: I only inform you as I heard."
"19495","Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, they said: Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, Abu al-Mundhir said in his hadith, he said: Habib ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: We used to recite in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold and silver he would seek another to them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"19496","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Hamzah, freedman of the Ansar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him."
"19497","Waki narrated to us, Israil and my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: How many campaigns did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, make, he said: Nineteen, and I raided with him seventeen, and he preceded me by two campaigns."
"19498","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin informed us, from Aidhillah al-Mujashii, from Abu Dawud, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: I said, or they said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these sacrifices, he said: The practice of your father Ibrahim, they said: What is for us therein, he said: For every hair a good deed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, and wool, he said: For every hair of wool a good deed."
"19499","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah narrating from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, Amr said: So I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he denied that and said: Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him."
"19500","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a campaign, and Abdillah ibn Ubayy said: If we return to Madinah the mightier will expel the humbler therefrom, he said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, he said: So Abdillah ibn Ubayy swore that nothing of that happened, he said: So my people blamed me and said: What did you intend by this, he said: So I went and slept grieved or sorrowful, he said: So the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to me, or I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Allah Almighty has revealed your excuse and confirmed you, he said: So this verse came down: They are those who say: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse, until reaching: If we return to Madinah the mightier will expel the humbler therefrom."
"19501","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies are attended, so when one of you enters, let him say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils. Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah informed me, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"19502","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Abdillah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had doors opening into the mosque. He said: One day he said: Close these doors except the door of Ali. He said: People talked about that. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, I was commanded to close these doors except the door of Ali, and your spokesmen said things about it. By Allah, I neither closed anything nor opened it, but I was commanded with something and I followed it."
"19503","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj the freedman of Banu Thalabah, from Qutbah ibn Malik, the uncle of Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shubah disparaged Ali, so Zayd ibn Arqam said: You know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid reviling the dead, so why do you revile Ali when he has died."
"19504","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, he said: I heard Abu Abdillah Maymun narrating from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to treat pleurisy with Indian costus and oil."
"19505","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Abdillah al-Shami, he said: I heard Muawiyah preaching, saying: O people of Sham, al-Ansari narrated to me - Shubah said, meaning Zayd ibn Arqam - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A party of my ummah will remain victorious upon the truth, and I hope that you are they, O people of Sham."
"19506","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, the freedman of the Ansar, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a stop where they stopped on his journey, and he said: You are not one part of a hundred thousand parts of those of my ummah who will come to me at the Hawd. He said: I said: How many were you that day. He said: We were seven hundred or eight hundred."
"19507","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard al-Nadr ibn Anas narrating from Zayd ibn Arqam that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"19508","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Dawud al-Tufawi narrating from Abu Muslim al-Bajali, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of his prayer: O Allah, our Lord and Lord of everything, I bear witness that You are the Lord alone with no partner for You. Ibrahim said, twice: Our Lord and Lord of everything, I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger. Our Lord and Lord of everything, I bear witness that all servants are brothers. O Allah, our Lord and Lord of everything, make me sincere to You, me and my family, in every hour of this world and the Hereafter, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, hear and answer. Allah is Greatest, the Greatest, Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth, Allah is Greatest, the Greatest, Allah suffices me and He is the best Disposer of affairs, Allah is Greatest, the Greatest."
"19509","Affan and Muammal both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qays ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ata, that Ibn Abbas said: O Zayd ibn Arqam, did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a limb of game while in ihram and did not accept it. He said: Yes. Muammal said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it and said: We are in ihram. He said: Yes."
"19510","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: When Abdullah ibn Ubayy said what he said, Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah, or he said, If we return to Madinah, I heard him, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Some people of the Ansar blamed me. And he came and swore he did not say that, so I returned home and slept. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, or it reached me and I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Allah has confirmed you as truthful and excused you. Then this verse was revealed: They are the ones who say, Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah."
"19511","My father said: Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"19512","Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Hamzah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"19513","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: How many campaigns did you fight with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Seventeen. He said: And Zayd ibn Arqam narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned nineteen times, and that he performed after emigrating one Hajj, the Farewell Hajj. Abu Ishaq said: And another in Makkah."
"19514","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, that Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to Anas ibn Malik at the time of al-Harrah consoling him for those killed among his children and his people, and said: I bring you glad tidings from Allah. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar, and forgive the women of the Ansar and the women of the sons of the Ansar and the women of the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"19515","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, he said: I prayed behind Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and he said the takbir five times. Abu Isa Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla stood up to him, took his hand, and said: Did you forget. He said: No, but I prayed behind Abu al-Qasim, my beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said the takbir five times, so I will never leave it."
"19516","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zarah, from Abu Salman al-Muadhdhin, he said: Abu Surayhah died, and Zayd ibn Arqam prayed over him and said the takbir over him four times, and said: So did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19517","Husayn ibn Muhammad and Abu Nuaym, with the same meaning, both said: Fitr narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, gathered the people in al-Rahbah, then said to them: I adjure every Muslim who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Ghadir Khumm what he heard, to stand when he stood. Thirty people stood - and Abu Nuaym said: Many people stood - and they testified when he took him by the hand and said to the people: Do you know that I am closer to the believers than themselves. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, this is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. He said: I left with something in my heart, so I met Zayd ibn Arqam and said to him: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying such-and-such. He said: Why do you deny it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that to him."
"19518","Husayn narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, a man of the Ansar, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: The first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Amr said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he denied it and said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"19519","Husayn narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: When we came to him we said: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We have grown old and forgotten, and narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is grave."
"19520","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibn Abi Layla, he said: We said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Narrate to us. He said: We have grown old and forgotten, and narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is grave."
"19521","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Hamzah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Ali ibn Abi Talib. I mentioned that to al-Nakhai, and he denied it and said: Abu Bakr was the first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19522","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar mentioning from Abu al-Minhal that Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them, were partners. They bought silver for cash and on credit. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded them: What was for cash, carry it out, and what was on credit, return it."
"19523","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, extreme old age, cowardice, miserliness, and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant my soul its piety and purify it, You are the best to purify it, You are its Guardian and Master. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble, a soul that is never satisfied, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not answered. He said: Zayd ibn Arqam said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them to us, and we teach them to you."
"19524","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, that he heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and we stopped at a stop, and I heard him say: You are not one part of a hundred thousand parts of those of my ummah who will come to me at the Hawd. He said: How many were you that day. He said: Seven hundred or eight hundred."
"19525","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal, he said: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam about exchange. One says: Ask this one, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable, and the other says: Ask this one, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable. He said: I asked them both, and both say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for gold on credit. And I asked this one, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for gold on credit."
"19526","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qays informed us, from Ata, that Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Zayd ibn Arqam, did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a limb of game while in ihram and did not accept it. He said: Yes indeed."
"19527","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jafar al-Ahmar informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Hakim, he said: I prayed behind Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and he said the takbir five times, then he turned and said: So did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say the takbir, or: your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19528","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Ali ibn Rabiah, he said: I met Zayd ibn Arqam while he was entering to al-Mukhtar or leaving him, and I said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am leaving among you the Two Weighty Things. He said: Yes."
"19529","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah al-Muhallimi, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: A man of Paradise is given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, desire, and intercourse. A man of the Jews said: One who eats and drinks needs to relieve himself. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: The need of one of them is sweat pouring from his skin, then his belly shrinks."
"19530","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub the freedman of Banu Thalabah, from Qutbah ibn Malik, he said: A commander reviled Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, so Zayd ibn Arqam stood and said: You know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade reviling the dead, so why do you revile Ali when he has died."
"19531","Waki narrated to us, Israil and my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: How many campaigns did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fight. He said: Nineteen, and I fought with him seventeen campaigns, and he preceded me by two campaigns."
"19532","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar and Amir ibn Musab informed me that they heard Abu al-Minhal say: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam, and they said: We were traders at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about exchange, and he said: If it is hand to hand, there is no harm, and if it is on credit, it is not proper."
"19533","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Iyas ibn Abi Ramlah al-Shami, he said: I witnessed Muawiyah ask Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you witness with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two Eids coinciding. He said: Yes. He prayed the Eid early in the day, then gave a concession for the Jumuah, saying: Whoever wishes to attend the congregation, let him attend."
"19534","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, that Zayd ibn Arqam saw people praying Duha in the mosque of Quba and said: They know that prayer at another hour is better. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat."
"19535","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Zayd used to say the takbir over our funerals four times, and he said it over a funeral five times. I asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say it."
"19536","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Hamzah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not a part of a hundred thousand, or of seventy thousand, of those who will come to me at the Hawd. He said: They asked him: How many were you. He said: Eight hundred or seven hundred."
"19537","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"19538","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah informed me, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"19539","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, he said: We said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Narrate to us. He said: We have grown old and forgotten, and narration concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is grave."
"19540","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Ubayd, from Maymun Abu Abdillah, he said: Zayd ibn Arqam said, while I listened: We stopped with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a valley called Wadi Khumm. He commanded the prayer and prayed it in the midday heat. He said: He addressed us, and shade was made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a garment on a samurah tree from the sun. He said: Do you not know, or do you not bear witness, that I am closer to every believer than himself. They said: Yes. He said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, oppose whoever opposes him and befriend whoever befriends him."
"19541","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal, a man of Banu Kinanah, he said: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam. He said: I asked one, and he said: Go to so-and-so, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable, and I asked the other, and he said the like of that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for gold on credit."
"19542","Ali ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Abdillah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribing oil and wars for pleurisy. Qatadah said: He pours it as ladud from the side he complains of."
"19543","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Abdillah, he said: I was with Zayd ibn Arqam when a man came from the farthest part of the fustat and asked him about an ailment, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Am I not closer to the believers than themselves. They said: Yes. He said: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. Maymun said: Some people narrated to me from Zayd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"19544","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ajlah, from al-Shabi, from Abd Khayr al-Hadrami, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was in Yemen when a woman was brought to whom three men had intercourse in one purity period. He asked two: Do you concede the child to this one. They did not concede. Then he asked two: Do you concede the child to this one. They did not concede. Then he kept asking two about one until he finished asking two by two about one, and they did not concede. Then he cast lots among them, attached the child to whom the lot fell, and imposed on him two-thirds of the diyah. That was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he laughed until his molars showed."
"19545","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Hasan ibn Muslim informed us, from Abu al-Minhal - but he did not hear it from him - that he heard Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib say: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about exchange: If it is hand to hand, there is no harm; if it is on credit, it is not proper."
"19546","Asbat narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies are attended, so when one of you wants to enter, let him say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."
"19547","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies are attended, so when one of you enters the privy, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from male and female devils."
"19548","Yahya ibn Adam and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr both said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say - Ibn Abi Bukayr said: from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: I went out with my uncle on a campaign and heard Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul saying to his companions: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah, and if we return to Madinah the mightier will expel the humbler. I mentioned that to my uncle, and my uncle mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to me, and I told him. He sent to Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul and his companions, and they swore they did not say it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared me untruthful and believed him. A grief befell me the like of which never befell me, and I sat at home. My uncle said: You only wanted that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declare you untruthful and dislike you. He said: Until Allah revealed: When the hypocrites come to you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to me and recited it, then said: Allah has confirmed you as truthful."
"19549","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, that he heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and the people suffered hardship. Abdullah ibn Ubayy said to his companions: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse from around him, and said: If we return to Madinah the mightier will expel the humbler. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him that. He sent to Abdullah ibn Ubayy and asked him, and he exerted his oath that he did not do it. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared Zayd untruthful. He said: What they said fell upon my heart, until Allah revealed my confirmation in: When the hypocrites come to you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them to seek forgiveness for them, but they twisted their heads. And His saying: As if they were propped timbers. He said: They were the most handsome of men."
"19550","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I met Zayd ibn Arqam and said to him: How many campaigns did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fight. He said: Nineteen. I said: How many did you fight with him. He said: Seventeen campaigns. He said: I said: What was the first campaign he fought. He said: Dhat al-Ushayr, or al-Ushayrah."
"19551","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, he said: The Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, every prophet has followers, and we have followed you, so supplicate Allah to make our followers from us. He said: He supplicated for them that He make their followers from them. He said: I conveyed that to Ibn Abi Layla, and he said: Zayd, meaning Ibn Arqam, claimed that."
"19552","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd narrating from al-Nadr ibn Anas, he said: A son of Anas died, and Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"19553","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib, he said: I heard Abu al-Minhal, a man of Banu Kinanah, he said: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib about exchange, and he said: Ask Zayd ibn Arqam, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable. He said: I asked Zayd, and he said: Ask al-Bara, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable. He said: Both said together: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for gold on credit."
"19554","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Abdillah, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought nineteen campaigns, and I fought with him seventeen campaigns."
"19555","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Matar, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad doubted the Hawd, so he sent to Zayd ibn Arqam and asked him about the Hawd. He narrated to him a well-adorned hadith that pleased him. He said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: No, but my brother narrated it to me."
"19556","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, he said: Zayd ibn Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas used to ask him to recall: How did you tell me about meat. Ibn Bakr said: given to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while unlawful, and Abd al-Razzaq said: given to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, he was given a limb - Ibn Bakr said: a leg, a limb of game meat - and he returned it to him and said: We do not eat it; we are in ihram."
"19557","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ajlah, from al-Shabi, from Abdillah ibn Abi al-Khalil, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that some men had intercourse with a woman in one purity, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to two of them: Do you willingly concede to this one. They said: No. He turned to the other two and said: Do you willingly concede to this one. They said: No. He said: You are quarreling partners. I will cast lots among you; whomever the lot falls upon, I impose on him two-thirds of the diyah and attach the child to him. He said: That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I know nothing except what Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said."
"19558","Yazid informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Bakr ibn Anas, he said: Zayd ibn Arqam wrote to Anas ibn Malik consoling him for those stricken among his children and his people on the day of al-Harrah, and wrote to him: I bring you glad tidings from Allah. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar, and the women of the Ansar and the women of the sons of the Ansar and the women of the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"19559","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Ajlah informed us, from al-Shabi, from Abu al-Khalil, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought three men when he was in Yemen who shared in a child. He cast lots among them, imposed on whom the lot fell two-thirds of the diyah, and gave the child to him. Zayd ibn Arqam said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of the judgment of Ali, and he laughed until his molars showed."
"19560","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Khalid Abu al-Ala al-Khaffaf, from Atiyyah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I enjoy when the Bearer of the Horn has taken the Horn, bent his forehead, and listened attentively for when he will be commanded. He said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and it weighed upon them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: Allah suffices us and He is the best Disposer of affairs."
"19561","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Khalid ibn Tahman Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned its meaning."
"19562","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque of Quba, or entered the mosque of Quba after the sun had risen, and they were praying. He said: The prayer of the oft-returning, they used to pray it when the young camels feel the heat."
"19563","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, and Ismail ibn Umar said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: Ophthalmia afflicted me and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me. He said: When I recovered I went out. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What if your eyes were as they were, what would you do. He said: I said: If my eyes were as they were, I would be patient and seek reward. He said: If your eyes were as they were and then you were patient and sought reward, you would meet Allah with no sin upon you. Ismail said: Then you were patient and sought reward, Allah would make Paradise obligatory for you."
